      "problem": "Given that $f(x)=\\frac{5{x}^{2}}{9x-7}$, find ${f}^{′}(x).$",
      "worked_solution": "The numerator and denominator are $u(x)=5{x}^{2}$ and $v(x)=9x-7,$ respectively. Their derivatives are given by\n\n \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{u}^{′}(x) & =10x, \\\\ {v}^{′}(x) & =9.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & =\\frac{{u}^{′}(x)\\cdot v(x)-u(x){v}^{′}(x)}{[v(x)]^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{10x\\cdot (9x-7)-(5{x}^{2})\\cdot 9}{{(9x-7)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{90{x}^{2}-70x-45{x}^{2}}{{(9x-7)}^{2}} \\\\  & =\\frac{45{x}^{2}-70x}{{(9x-7)}^{2}}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
